<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Klooga concentration camp</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Klooga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camp</a> was a Nazi labour camp in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, a subcamp of Vaivara, which operated from 1943 to 1944. It held mainly Jewish prisoners deported from the ghettos of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> and elsewhere. On 19 September 1944, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> approached, the SS shot and burned about 2,000 prisoners, one of the largest massacres of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> in Estonia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/klooga-concentration-camp.jpg" alt="Klooga concentration camp" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Soosaar · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corpses_found_at_Klooga_concentration_camp_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
